  "files": [
   "party/box-party.js",
   "party/game-library.js"
  ],
  "notes": "Box Party is the metagame: a CSS 3D flyover of mystery boxes, then name entry, then each box launches a minigame and the coin tally updates. It must drive the other ported games through the new platform:\n- QUEUE used window.GAMES (game-library.js) entries. Use manifest entries instead: IGB.find(id), whose .name and .box ({ color, bg, note, name }) are the cube skin. The queue becomes [['coconut-climbers','mystery-maze'],['soccer-heads','volley-heads'],['bongo-bounce','melody-match'],['coin-chaos'],['painter-panic','cardboard-cutout','stubble-trouble'],['milkers','popcorn-panhandlers'],['plummet-panic','cookie-cutter'],['coin-chaos'],['find-my-meep','town-fair'],['goal-patrol','bowling-bonanza'],['final-frenzy']]. (The old library pointed Goal Patrol at GoalieGame from goalie.js, which was never loaded, so that box was broken; goal-patrol is the right game. List it under bugFixes.)\n- Launch a minigame with IGB.start(entry.id, $minigame, players) (it returns a promise of the instance), and catch its completion with const restore = IGB.handleComplete(doCompleteGame) instead of setting window.doPartyGameComplete. On completion (and on SKIP MINIGAME) stop it with IGB.stop(instance), which runs its fini and removes its stage, then restore() the handler.\n- Name entry: IGB.start('name-entry', <container>, players, finiNameEntry); stop it with IGB.stop when done.\n- setPlayers forwards to the scene and to the live minigame, as before.\n- The 3D world (partyScene3D, partyWorld3D, partyPlane3D, the track SVG, mountains, pop explosions) is a genuine CSS 3D scene: keep it DOM in stage.$bg with its CSS in games/box-party.css (manifest already has css: true), every selector scoped under igb-stage[game=\"box-party\"]. PartyCube3D and BoxPartyCube now live in shared/cube.js as Cube3D and BoxCube (read it; BoxCube takes a manifest entry as its game). The old rule `partyScene3D partycube3DSurface { border: 10px solid #ffdd00; box-sizing: border-box }` becomes a scoped rule on cube-surface. Meeps standing on the 3D plane become MeepView (DOM) with the same CSS transforms.\n- Layering, as in the old DOM: the minigame container sits below Box Party's HUD (its debug buttons stay visible over a running minigame) and above the scene; the white overlay flash and the name entry sit on top. A suggested arrangement: stage.$bg holds [$minigame, scene]; stage.$ui holds [hud, tally, overlay, name entry]. The scene is hidden while a minigame runs, as before.\n- Box Party has no canvas art of its own unless you find some worth moving; its draw can be omitted.\n- Its intervals (scene step at 30 fps, resize loop) become stage.interval; the resize loop goes entirely.\n- For the end-to-end check, run box-party with --speed=4 and enough seconds to reach the first minigame launch; confirm the minigame starts inside Box Party, and use the HUD's SKIP MINIGAME debug button (button text) via --eval to confirm the tally updates and play moves on. Other games may still be mid-port in parallel when you run; a game whose file is missing just fails to launch, so note it rather than chase it.",
